Everything in rules/ — `rules.v1.json`, the canonical gp.v1 JSON of one
`RulesTable`, and the notes that go with it — is licensed under either of

  * MIT License            (../LICENSES/MIT.txt)
  * Apache License, 2.0    (../LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

at your option. The shape of this file is schema and its values are data
(decisions log section 2.7 item 78): the numbers here are what an estimate is
made of, so an alternative verifier, planner or playbook generator has to be
able to read the same table to reach the same answer the game reaches. That is
the same reason proto/ is permissive, and it is why this directory does not
take the game's copyleft even though the sim is the thing that consumes it.

`rules.v1.json` cannot carry a comment, so it has a `rules.v1.json.license`
sidecar beside it as well; ../REUSE.toml covers the directory either way.

Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for
inclusion in this directory shall be dual licensed as above, with no additional
terms or conditions, and signed off under the Developer Certificate of Origin
1.1 (../docs/DCO.txt).

The repository-wide scheme is described in ../LICENSE and ../docs/LICENSING.md;
the machine-readable manifest is ../REUSE.toml.
